   "postDate": "2026-08-17T10:12:27.983Z",
   "rawMarkdown": "There are several (7 if I recall/count correctly) training studies where both knees are in the DICOM.\n\nThis first caused my very naive crop to show no knee. Now I am wondering if we have some interesting chance to have some clean knees. \n\nFor example: ACL is unlikely to affect both knees, right? I do not think people typically tear both. Has anyone tried labelling and training on the good knees?\n\n",
   "content": "<p>There are several (7 if I recall/count correctly) training studies where both knees are in the DICOM.</p>\n<p>This first caused my very naive crop to show no knee. Now I am wondering if we have some interesting chance to have some clean knees. </p>\n<p>For example: ACL is unlikely to affect both knees, right? I do not think people typically tear both. Has anyone tried labelling and training on the good knees?</p>",
